!*********************************** Marker Types ********************************************************************
!Co-dominant marker: When heterozygote F1 is present, P1 is coded as 2, F1 is coded as 1, and P2 is coded as 0; Otherwise, P1 is coded as 2, and P2 is coded as 0. 
!Dominant marker: When heterozygote F1 is present, P1 and F1 are coded as 12, and P2 is coded as 0; Otherwise, P1 is coded as 2, and P2 is coded as 0. 
!Recessive markers: When heterozygote F1 is present, P1 is coded as 2, and F1 and P2 are coded as 10; Otherwise, P1 is coded as 2, and P2 is coded as 0. 
!Missing marker is coded as -1. 
